Local patch for OpenStack Trove guest agent (branch stable/2026.1).

Bug:
  Trove's trove/common/cfg.py registers a `percona` OptGroup, but — unlike
  the `mysql` and `mariadb` groups — its option list (percona_opts) does NOT
  define `docker_image` / `backup_docker_image`. Since the Victoria "datastore
  as a docker container" model, the guest agent selects the engine container
  in trove/guestagent/datastore/mysql_common/service.py start_db() with:

      docker_image = CONF.get(CONF.datastore_manager).docker_image

  For a `percona` datastore (registered with manager=percona so the guest
  reads the [percona] section and runs percona-server rather than mysql), that
  resolves to CONF.get("percona").docker_image and raises:

      oslo_config.cfg.NoSuchOptError: no such option docker_image in group
      [percona]

  which aborts prepare with "Failed to prepare datastore ... group [percona]"
  and the instance lands in ERROR / "failed to spawn".

Fix:
  Add docker_image / backup_docker_image to percona_opts (mirroring the mysql
  group), so the guest reads them from the [percona] section of
  trove-guestagent.conf (rendered by the trove_enablement_techpreview role as
  docker_image=percona/percona-server and
  backup_docker_image=percona/percona-server-backup).
  The mysql group is untouched, so the `mysql` and `percona` datastores stay
  independent and can coexist.

Upstream:
  This is a genuine upstream gap. It is suitable to propose to openstack/trove
  (add the containerized-datastore options to the percona group). Until merged
  upstream, it is applied locally against the guest-agent source clone.

This file is applied inside the disk-image-create build chroot (against the
guest-agent clone at /opt/guest-agent) by the debian-guest element's
pre-install.d/12-percona-cfg-docker-image script, BEFORE install.d pip-installs
/opt/guest-agent. Paths are relative to the trove repo root, so it applies with
`git apply -p1` or `patch -p1`.

--- a/trove/common/cfg.py
+++ b/trove/common/cfg.py
@@ -629,6 +629,17 @@
     'percona', title='Percona options',
     help="Oslo option group designed for Percona datastore")
 percona_opts = [
+    # GENESTACK: percona datastore runs as a docker container; these options
+    # are absent from the upstream percona group. Without docker_image the
+    # guest agent raises NoSuchOptError in mysql_common/service.py start_db()
+    # for a percona datastore. Values are supplied by the [percona] section of
+    # trove-guestagent.conf (docker_image=percona/percona-server).
+    cfg.StrOpt('docker_image', default='percona/percona-server',
+               help='Database docker image (GENESTACK: Percona datastore).'),
+    cfg.StrOpt('backup_docker_image',
+               sample_default='your-registry/your-repo/db-backup-percona',
+               help='The docker image used for backup and restore '
+                    '(GENESTACK: Percona datastore).'),
     cfg.StrOpt('database_service_uname', default='database',
                help='The name of database service user.'),
     cfg.StrOpt('database_service_uid',
